From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/36] Test the ComfyUI backend against a fixture and a fake
 server
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is no ComfyUI here, so the live round trip is unexercised. Everything
that does not need one is covered: every shipped template parses, every
binding resolves, and every node class and input name it uses exists in an
/object_info fixture built from ComfyUI's own node definitions — which is
the check an invented class or input cannot survive.

Then the behaviour that would rot silently: node ids identical across two
submissions of one recipe, and unchanged when a region is added; pruning
that reconnects the chain instead of leaving a dangling link; a missing node
pack reported by pack name and never submitted; a missing model offering the
nearest installed file; and submit to progress to history to bytes against a
fake server, with a socket, without one, when the socket drops, when the
finish event arrives while the poll it should shorten is still in flight,
when the prompt is rejected, and when the user cancels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
